# Government Software Context

When building features, consider the government domain context in `context/`.

## User Personas (context/personas.md)

Design for varying technical abilities:

| Role | Tech Level | Design Approach |
|------|-----------|-----------------|
| Maintenance Worker | Low | Simple interfaces, large touch targets, mobile-first |
| Permit Reviewer | Mid | Efficient workflows, progressive disclosure |
| Budget Director | Mid | Cross-department views, scenario planning |
| IT Director | High | Keyboard shortcuts, bulk operations, integrations |

## Product Suites (context/suite-scope.md)

| Suite | Purpose | Key Features |
|-------|---------|--------------|
| B&P | Budgeting & Planning | Proposals, approvals, scenario planning |
| EAM | Asset Management | Work orders, inspections, GIS mapping |
| PLC | Permitting & Licensing | Intake, review, payment, inspection workflow |
| PRO | Procurement | Solicitations, vendor management, contracts |
| FIN | Financials | GL, AP, AR, Payroll, Purchasing |

## Design Guidelines

### For Low-Tech Users
- Clear visual hierarchy
- Minimal cognitive load
- Large click/touch targets
- Simple navigation
- Avoid technical jargon

### For Mid-Tech Users
- Efficient workflows
- Progressive disclosure of advanced features
- Keyboard + mouse support
- Contextual help

### For High-Tech Users
- Keyboard shortcuts
- Bulk operations
- API/integration capabilities
- Power user features

### Mobile Considerations
- Field workers (Maintenance, Inspectors) need mobile-optimized interfaces
- Offline capability for fieldwork
- Camera/location integration for inspections

## Domain Terminology

Use government-appropriate language:
- "Citizen" or "Applicant" (not "User")
- "Department" or "Agency" (not "Team")
- "Fiscal Year" (not "Calendar Year" for budgets)
- "Work Order" (not "Ticket")
- "Solicitation" (not "Bid Request")
